{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838806-soulsteel-promethean-character-concept","id":838806,"title":"Soulsteel Promethean character concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-28T14:27:57-08:00","id":838806,"title":"Soulsteel Promethean character concept","content":"So I've been working on a character concept for a Promethean villain, and I'm not entirely sure how to execute it. The idea is that he's sort of a golem forged of Soulsteel (constructed by a mad ghost in the deep Underworld) and animated by the Divine Fire, and he finds this state to be extremely agreeable. He's a character who literally does not care that he inflicts horrible things upon everyone he touches. In fact, he sees this as a positive; Disquiet and Wasteland are the gifts he brings as he spreads a gospel of despair. He wields them as weapons to drive humans mad. To poison their lands and their minds. &quot;Men advise one another to see him, and shudder. And where he goes, rest vanishes, for the small hours are rent with the screams of nightmare...&quot;<br /> <br /> He is explicitly a monster, and I intend to pit a group of player characters against him at some point. He believes that becoming human is not a matter of bringing himself up but of bringing the human condition itself down; humanity must be made to cast off its delusions of morality, of uniqueness, and accept that they too are monsters no better than he. What I'm not sure of is how to best represent this given the rules we have. Would this be... Tammuz? Just of alternate construction? Osiran? Hmm. At first I was tempted to make him Centimani, but I'm not so sure that's appropriate after reading up on them. He's not a creature of flux, and he's no mutant; but he's literally infecting people with disquiet and spreading wastelands on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:29:56-08:00","id":838808,"title":"","content":"Sounds like an Unfleshed Centimanus to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:35:10-08:00","id":838813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838806-soulsteel-promethean-character-concept?p=838808#post838808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like an Unfleshed Centimanus to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaah, cool. In which book would I find the rules for the Unfleshed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:20:57-08:00","id":838827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838806-soulsteel-promethean-character-concept?p=838813#post838813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aaah, cool. In which book would I find the rules for the Unfleshed?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e has them in Saturnine Night, the last major sourcebook for the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:21:59-08:00","id":838828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838806-soulsteel-promethean-character-concept?p=838813#post838813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aaah, cool. In which book would I find the rules for the Unfleshed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Saturnine Night, same book as the Zeka. They're in Chapter two, to be precise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T16:31:48-08:00","id":838856,"title":"","content":"Excellent. I'll buy a copy and peruse. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T18:00:23-08:00","id":838885,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Horror Recognition Guide (and the Collection of Horrors that goes with it) describes a similar character, one Oleg Chernek. He's a Zeky arms dealer whose end goal is a global nuclear exchange; you might mine him for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:57:39-08:00","id":839132,"title":"","content":"If he is from the Underworld stuff, maybe Ulgan will work also as Lineage? It's Ephemera as fluid - most of the time it's think that it's from spirits, but I think that &quot;ghosts stuff&quot; would also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T10:44:36-08:00","id":841987,"title":"","content":"1e Unfleshed basically work out as &quot;your choice of Disquiet and Torment from the other lines, but with a unique Wasteland&quot;. So an Unfleshed with Ulgan Disquiet and/or Torment could work out as the best of both worlds, especially if you apply the Ulgan traits as-is rather than tweaking them as per the book.<br /> <br /> An alternative, of course, is to make your character an Ulgan Construct - that's an Ulgan Promethean whose body is made of inanimate material, an option covered by the Magnum Opus sourcebook. They basically gain +2 Armor for -2 Speed and potentially unique benefits depending on the material they're made of; wood or other flammable materials (wax, plastic, paper) are given as one example, doubling Fire damage but halving Bashing damage. So that's an option as well, if you can figure out how soulsteel might affect physical traits, Disquiet and/or Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}